# Copy to .env and adjust. Paths are relative to the /server folder.
PORT=4000
# CHANGE THIS in production
JWT_SECRET=please-change-me
# Platform admin page at /admin (keep it secret)
ADMIN_KEY=change-me-admin-key
# Public sign-up is closed by default. Set to 1 only to re-open it.
# ALLOW_REGISTER=0
# WhatsApp Cloud API (Meta) — needed for stores whose auto-WhatsApp switch is on
# WA_TOKEN=
# WA_PHONE_ID=
# WA_TEMPLATE=new_order
# WA_TEMPLATE_LANG=ar
# DB_FILE=./data/souqna.db
# MEDIA_DIR=./data/media
# Point at your CDN (e.g. Cloudflare R2 / S3 + CloudFront) once media is synced there
MEDIA_BASE_URL=/media

# --- Security (set before launch) ---
# Two-step confirmation for /admin. Generate with: npm run admin-totp -w server, then add the line it prints.
# ADMIN_TOTP_SECRET=
# Daily backup of the database + photos. Point at a folder on a persistent disk / synced drive.
# BACKUP_DIR=./backups
# BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS=14
# Seed only: password / phone for the Town Style demo store (random password is printed if omitted)
# TOWNSTYLE_PASSWORD=
# TOWNSTYLE_PHONE=
# Account whose dashboard is read-only for "Try the dashboard"
# DEMO_EMAIL=ahmed@banhalook.app

# --- Push notifications (VAPID keys are generated automatically and stored in the DB; set only to pin them) ---
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com

# --- WhatsApp alerts to the Banha Outfit team (needs the WhatsApp Cloud API above) ---
# PLATFORM_WA=201067378110
# WA_PLATFORM_TEMPLATE=platform_delivery
# WA_SERVICE_TEMPLATE=service_request

# --- Cloudflare R2 photo storage (optional, free up to 10 GB). Set all five to store new photos on R2 instead of the volume.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET=
# R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://pub-xxxxxxxx.r2.dev

# --- Off-site database backups (optional). Use a separate PRIVATE bucket, e.g. banha-backups.
# The bucket must differ from R2_BUCKET. R2_ACCOUNT_ID and the standard R2 S3 keys above are required.
# BACKUP_R2_BUCKET=banha-backups
# Optional dedicated S3 keys for the backup bucket; otherwise R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID / R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY are reused.
# BACKUP_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# BACKUP_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2 S3 keys must have write access to the backup bucket. CF_AI_TOKEN is not an R2 credential.
# R2 backup contains the database only; BACKUP_DIR on a persistent disk is needed to back up photos.

# --- Visual search model. "clip" = FREE local computer vision (CLIP via ONNX): understands the item type, detects several
# pieces in an outfit photo, learns from your own catalogue and only shows genuinely similar products. No API key, photos stay
# on the server. NO persistent volume: the model (~150 MB) is stored in your Cloudflare R2 bucket (needs the R2_* variables above)
# and copied to the container's temporary disk at start-up. The first start downloads it from HuggingFace and uploads it to R2
# automatically (or run `npm run model:prefetch -w server` once). Needs ~400 MB RAM. If it cannot load, the built-in colour
# model keeps working automatically. Default (unset) = colour model. After deploying: npm run train:visual -w server -- --apply
# VISUAL_MODEL=clip
# VISUAL_CLIP_MODEL=Xenova/clip-vit-base-patch32
#   fashion-tuned alternative: VISUAL_CLIP_MODEL=Marqo/marqo-fashionCLIP  (ViT-B/16: needs more RAM + R2 space, often fp32/fp16 only)
#   decide with data:  npm run compare:visual -w server   (compares models on YOUR products, writes nothing)
# MODEL_CACHE_DIR=/app/.model-cache   (temporary folder, already set in the Dockerfile)

# --- Hosted visual-search providers (pick one in admin -> النظام -> البحث بالصورة)
# JINA_API_KEY=            # jina.ai (jina-clip-v2) - hosted CLIP, no RAM on our server
# CF_ACCOUNT_ID=           # Cloudflare account id (falls back to R2_ACCOUNT_ID)
# CF_AI_TOKEN=             # Cloudflare API token with "Workers AI" permission (Read)
# CF_R2_METRICS_TOKEN=      # Cloudflare API token with Workers R2 Storage Read permission

# Stylist chat ("مودة") — pick ONE provider
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# STYLIST_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
# or free-tier Cloudflare Workers AI: CF_ACCOUNT_ID + CF_AI_TOKEN
